WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.130
- You found a photo from your first

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:01.963
table read that you all did?

00:00:01.963 --> 00:00:02.910
- Oh, yes.
- Oh yes yeah.

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:05.229
- Yes, our casting
director, Allison Jones,

00:00:05.229 --> 00:00:08.130
brought her camera and
she took a Polaroid of us

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:09.500
and she gave one to each of us.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.210
And I've saved mine all these years.

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:13.350
- That's so cool, we do
Polaroids on this show.

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:14.183
I love it.

00:00:14.183 --> 00:00:15.016
It just looks vintage and cool.

00:00:15.016 --> 00:00:17.380
- I didn't get one because
I wasn't there that day.

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:18.270
- She hadn't been cast yet.

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:19.610
- I hadn't been cast yet.

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:21.200
- [Kelly] That is so.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.060
- I'm okay with it.

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:23.120
- Wasn't it funny though?

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:24.680
Aren't you, Angela, you tried out right,

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:25.600
when everyone auditioning,

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:26.880
you auditioned for her part, right?

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.300
- I auditioned for the role of Pam

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.900
and I went in you guys,

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.120
and I thought I did so great.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:34.680
And it was a big room.

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:36.190
- You did, you got the
job, just a different one.

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:37.023
- I got a different job.

00:00:37.023 --> 00:00:38.850
But, it was a room full of people

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:43.630
and there's a moment where
Michael is fake firing Pam

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:46.610
in front of Ryan the temp,
to like pull a prank.

00:00:46.610 --> 00:00:49.990
And Pam starts to cry
and calls him a jerk.

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:51.660
And I called him like a jerk,

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:53.130
and everyone started laughing.

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:55.231
And I was like, "I don't
think that was supposed to be

00:00:55.231 --> 00:00:58.164
"a laugh, I think I missed something."

00:00:58.164 --> 00:01:00.820
And then of course, you
see this vulnerable moment

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:03.470
that Pam, as much as she
hates that job, she needs it.

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:06.150
And Jenna did such an
amazing job portraying that.

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:07.610
But, so they said I didn't get the part

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:10.030
because I was a little too feisty,

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:10.863
too feisty for Pam.

00:01:10.863 --> 00:01:12.130
- You were raised a bit in
Texas, so it's understood.

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:14.010
- I know, listen, I'll call someone a jerk

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:14.843
if they're a jerk.

00:01:14.843 --> 00:01:16.110
- I'll call someone something else, yeah.

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:17.510
- [Angela] Maybe.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.980
- It depends on the moment.

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:20.177
- But then they brought me back they said,

00:01:20.177 --> 00:01:23.940
"hey, we got kind of a judgy,
snarky lady in accounting."

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:25.630
And I said, "OK".

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:26.607
- That call's amazing.

00:01:26.607 --> 00:01:29.162
"Hey, you know who you'd be perfect for?"

00:01:29.162 --> 00:01:31.370
- The snarky lady.
- The snarky lady.

